IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Act 1947 (Singapore) -- an individual's income tax for one year of assessment: whether I am resident (s 2),
-- whether foreign income I receive is exempt (s 13(7A)), my earned income and spouse reliefs and their cap (ss 38, 39(1),
-- 39(2)(a), 39A), the rates on my chargeable income (s 42 and Second Schedule Part A Table 3; s 43(1)(b)), the relief
-- for a non-resident employee (s 40B), and the parenthood rebate (s 42A).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer -- a person, resident or not, whose income for one year of assessment is charged.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 11/9/2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ITA1947.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: what income is charged and from where (ss 10-12, beyond s 13(7A)); the other exemptions (s 13 and ss 13A-13X);
-- deductions and capital allowances (Parts 5, 6); statutory and assessable income (Parts 7-9) -- assessable income is an
-- input; every s 39 relief other than earned income and spouse (the Fifth Schedule child relief, CPF and life insurance,
-- course fees, and the rest); Tables 1 and 2 of the Second Schedule (years of assessment before 2024); companies, trustees
-- and executors; ss 40A, 40C, 40D; withholding (Part 12); tax credits (Parts 13, 14); every concessionary rate (ss 43A-43X).
-- Machinery (the Comptroller's appointment and powers, rules, the Board of Review's constitution) is out.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual taxpayer, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Act 1947 -- my tax for one year of assessment`

-- "year of assessment" (s 2): "the period of 12 months commencing on 1 January 1948, and each subsequent period of 12 months".
-- Gloss: the calendar year in which tax is assessed on the income of the year before it.

§§ `s 2 -- resident in Singapore`

-- s 2, "resident in Singapore" (a): "in relation to an individual, means a person who, in the year preceding the year of
-- assessment, resides in Singapore except for such temporary absences therefrom as may be reasonable and not inconsistent
-- with a claim by such person to be resident in Singapore, and includes a person who is physically present or who exercises
-- an employment (other than as a director of a company) in Singapore for 183 days or more during the year preceding the year
-- of assessment".
-- Gloss: resident if I live here (allowing reasonable trips away), or if I was here, or worked here other than as a
-- director, for 183 days or more in the year before the year of assessment. Whether an absence is "reasonable" is asked of me
-- as a fact; the Act does not define it.
DECLARE `Residence facts` HAS
    `I resided in Singapore in the preceding year apart from reasonable temporary absences` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days I was physically present in Singapore in the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
    `days I exercised an employment in Singapore in the preceding year other than as a director` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN f IS A `Residence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I resident in Singapore` IF
        f's `I resided in Singapore in the preceding year apart from reasonable temporary absences`
    OR  f's `days I was physically present in Singapore in the preceding year` AT LEAST 183
    OR  f's `days I exercised an employment in Singapore in the preceding year other than as a director` AT LEAST 183

§§ `s 13(7A) -- foreign income received in Singapore`

-- s 13(7A): "There is exempt from tax any income arising from sources outside Singapore and received in Singapore --
-- (a) by any individual who is not resident in Singapore; and (b) on or after 1 January 2004 by any individual who is
-- resident in Singapore if the Comptroller is satisfied that the tax exemption would be beneficial to the individual, but
-- excludes such income received by the individual through a partnership in Singapore."
-- Gloss: a non-resident's remitted foreign income is exempt outright; a resident's is exempt only if the Comptroller is
-- satisfied the exemption benefits them, and never if it comes in through a Singapore partnership. The Comptroller's
-- satisfaction is an input, never guessed. Receipt is taken to be on or after 1 January 2004 (the encoded years are 2024 on).
-- Inference: the partnership exclusion is read as attaching to limb (b) only, where it is printed.
GIVEN `I am resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I received it through a partnership in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Comptroller is satisfied the exemption would be beneficial to me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my foreign income received in Singapore exempt` IF
        NOT `I am resident in Singapore`
    OR  (    `the Comptroller is satisfied the exemption would be beneficial to me`
         AND NOT `I received it through a partnership in Singapore`)

§§ `ss 38, 39(1) -- earned income relief`

-- s 38: chargeable income is "the remainder of the person's assessable income for that year after the reliefs and deductions
-- allowed in this Part have been made".
-- s 39(1): "In the case of an individual resident in Singapore in the year of assessment, there is allowed a deduction, in
-- respect of earned income, which is -- (a) in the case of an individual not falling within any other paragraph, the sum of
-- $1,000 or the amount of the earned income; (b) without affecting any deduction allowable under paragraph (c) or (d), in the
-- case of an individual who ... was totally blind or had any physical or mental disability which permanently and severely
-- restricted the individual's capacity for work, the sum of $4,000 ...; (c) ... above 55 years of age but was not above 60
-- years of age, the sum of $6,000 ...; and (d) ... above 60 years of age, the sum of $8,000 or the amount of earned income,
-- whichever is less."
-- Gloss: a resident deducts the lesser of a fixed sum and their earned income; the sum rises with age and disability.
-- NOT COVERED: a disabled individual who is also above 55. Paragraph (b) applies "without affecting" (c) and (d), which can be
-- read as both deductions together or as the larger one; the text does not settle it, so the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN `I am resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `I was totally blind or permanently and severely disabled for work in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was above 55 years of age at some time in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was above 60 years of age at some time in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What earned income relief can I deduct` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I am resident in Singapore` THEN JUST 0
        IF     `I was totally blind or permanently and severely disabled for work in the preceding year`
           AND `I was above 55 years of age at some time in the preceding year` THEN NOTHING
        IF `I was above 60 years of age at some time in the preceding year` THEN JUST (`the lesser of` 8_000 `my earned income`)
        IF `I was above 55 years of age at some time in the preceding year` THEN JUST (`the lesser of` 6_000 `my earned income`)
        IF `I was totally blind or permanently and severely disabled for work in the preceding year`
           THEN JUST (`the lesser of` 4_000 `my earned income`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the lesser of` 1_000 `my earned income`)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `s 39(2)(a) -- spouse relief`

-- s 39(2): "In the case of an individual resident in Singapore in the year of assessment who, in the year immediately
-- preceding the year of assessment -- (a) had a spouse, living with or maintained by him or her, whose income was not more
-- than $4,000 in that year (where the year of assessment is between the years of assessment 2010 and 2024 (both years
-- inclusive)) or not more than $8,000 in that year (where the year of assessment is 2025 or any subsequent year of
-- assessment), there is allowed a deduction of $2,000".
-- Gloss: $2,000 off for a spouse I lived with or maintained whose own income was small; the income limit doubled from YA 2025.
-- A year of assessment before 2010 is not covered (the earlier text is not in the deposit): NOTHING.
GIVEN `the year of assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `I am resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse lived with me or was maintained by me in the preceding year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse's income in the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What spouse relief can I deduct` IS
    IF `the year of assessment` LESS THAN 2010 THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `I am resident in Singapore`
            AND `my spouse lived with me or was maintained by me in the preceding year`
            AND `my spouse's income in the preceding year` AT MOST `the spouse income limit for` `the year of assessment`
         THEN JUST 2_000
         ELSE JUST 0

GIVEN `the year of assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the spouse income limit for` `the year of assessment` MEANS
    IF `the year of assessment` AT MOST 2024 THEN 4_000 ELSE 8_000

§§ `s 39A -- the $80,000 cap, and chargeable income`

-- s 39A: "for the year of assessment 2018 and every subsequent year of assessment, the total amount of all deductions
-- allowable to any individual under section 39 must not exceed $80,000 for that year of assessment."
-- Gloss: however many reliefs I qualify for, they come to $80,000 at most.
GIVEN `the total of my section 39 reliefs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What can my section 39 reliefs come to at most` IS
    `the lesser of` `the total of my section 39 reliefs` 80_000

-- s 38 with s 39A. Inference: chargeable income does not go below nil.
GIVEN `my assessable income` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of my section 39 reliefs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my chargeable income` IS
    `the greater of` 0 (`my assessable income` MINUS `What can my section 39 reliefs come to at most` `the total of my section 39 reliefs`)

§§ `s 42 and Second Schedule Part A Table 3 -- the resident rates`

-- s 42(1): tax is levied "upon the chargeable income of every person (other than a body of persons, a company, a person not
-- resident in Singapore, a trustee who is not the trustee of an incapacitated person, or an executor), ... in accordance
-- with the rates specified in Part A of the Second Schedule".
-- Second Schedule, Part A, Table 3: "RATES OF TAX ON CHARGEABLE INCOME OF AN INDIVIDUAL FOR YEAR OF ASSESSMENT 2024 AND
-- SUBSEQUENT YEARS OF ASSESSMENT" -- "For every dollar of the first $20,000 Nil" ... "For every dollar exceeding
-- $1,000,000 24%."
-- Gloss: progressive bands; each band's rate applies only to the dollars inside it.
DECLARE Band HAS
    `the next` IS A NUMBER
    `rate`     IS A NUMBER

`Table 3` MEANS
    --                  for every dollar of the next,  rate
    LIST
        (Band OF    20_000,      0),
        (Band OF    10_000,     2%),
        (Band OF    10_000,   3.5%),
        (Band OF    40_000,     7%),
        (Band OF    40_000,  11.5%),
        (Band OF    40_000,    15%),
        (Band OF    40_000,    18%),
        (Band OF    40_000,    19%),
        (Band OF    40_000,  19.5%),
        (Band OF    40_000,    20%),
        (Band OF   180_000,    22%),
        (Band OF   500_000,    23%)

-- "For every dollar exceeding $1,000,000 24%."
`Table 3 rate above the last band` MEANS 24%

GIVEN income IS A NUMBER
      bands  IS A LIST OF Band
      top    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax across` income bands top MEANS
    CONSIDER bands
    WHEN EMPTY THEN income TIMES top
    WHEN b FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF income AT MOST b's `the next`
        THEN income TIMES b's `rate`
        ELSE b's `the next` TIMES b's `rate` PLUS `the tax across` (income MINUS b's `the next`) rest top

-- Years of assessment before 2024 use Tables 1 and 2, which this encoding does not carry: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the year of assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `my chargeable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my tax at the resident rates` IS
    IF `the year of assessment` AT LEAST 2024
    THEN JUST (`the tax across` `my chargeable income` `Table 3` `Table 3 rate above the last band`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 43(1)(b) -- the non-resident rate`

-- s 43(1)(b): tax upon the chargeable income of "every individual not resident in Singapore -- (i) for the year of assessment
-- 2023 or a preceding year of assessment, tax at the rate of 22% on every dollar of the chargeable income thereof; and
-- (ii) for the year of assessment 2024 and subsequent years of assessment, tax at the rate of 24%".
-- Gloss: a non-resident pays one flat rate on every dollar, with no tax-free band.
GIVEN `the year of assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the non-resident rate for` `the year of assessment` IS
    IF `the year of assessment` AT MOST 2023 THEN 22% ELSE 24%

§§ `s 40B -- relief for a non-resident employee`

-- s 40B(1): applies to a person "not resident in Singapore and who derives income from the exercise of any employment in
-- Singapore", whose income does not include "(a) any withdrawal from the person's SRS account ...; or (b) income derived as a
-- public entertainer".
-- (2) relief "(a) where the only source of income in Singapore is such activity as a non-resident employee, by reduction of
-- the rate of tax to 15% on every dollar of the chargeable income; (b) where such person possesses any other source of income
-- in Singapore and the total assessable income exceeds the statutory income attributable to such activity ..., by reduction
-- of the rate of tax to 15% on such part of the chargeable income as bears the same proportion to the total chargeable income
-- as the statutory income attributable to such activity ... bears to the total assessable income; (c) ... the total
-- assessable income is equal to or less than the statutory income attributable to such activity ..., by reduction of the
-- rate of tax to 15% on every dollar of the chargeable income."
-- (3): "the tax payable in respect of such income must not be less than that which would be payable by a resident of Singapore
-- in the same circumstances."
-- (5): "non-resident employee" "excludes a director of a company".
-- Gloss: a non-resident employee pays 15% on the employment share of their chargeable income and the non-resident rate on the
-- rest, but never less than a resident would pay.
-- Inference: the s 40B(3) floor is applied to the whole tax, by comparing with Table 3 on the chargeable income a resident
-- would have in the same circumstances (an input, since it depends on reliefs a resident could claim; s 40B(3A) applies
-- the s 39A cap to it). A director is outside s 40B and pays the flat s 43(1)(b) rate. An SRS withdrawal or public
-- entertainer income takes the case to ss 40A, 40C or 40D, which are not encoded: NOTHING. A year before 2024: NOTHING.
DECLARE `Non-resident employment facts` HAS
    `the year of assessment` IS A NUMBER
    `I am a director of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have an SRS withdrawal or public entertainer income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my only source of income in Singapore is my employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my statutory income from the employment` IS A NUMBER
    `my total assessable income` IS A NUMBER
    `my chargeable income` IS A NUMBER
    `the chargeable income a resident would have in the same circumstances` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN f IS A `Non-resident employment facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my tax as a non-resident employee` IS
    BRANCH
        IF f's `the year of assessment` LESS THAN 2024 THEN NOTHING
        IF f's `I have an SRS withdrawal or public entertainer income` THEN NOTHING
        IF f's `I am a director of a company` THEN JUST (f's `my chargeable income` TIMES 24%)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the greater of` `the relieved tax` `the resident floor`)
    WHERE
        `the 15% share` MEANS
            IF     f's `my only source of income in Singapore is my employment`
                OR f's `my total assessable income` AT MOST f's `my statutory income from the employment`
            THEN f's `my chargeable income`
            ELSE f's `my chargeable income` TIMES f's `my statutory income from the employment` DIVIDED BY f's `my total assessable income`
        `the relieved tax` MEANS
            `the 15% share` TIMES 15% PLUS (f's `my chargeable income` MINUS `the 15% share`) TIMES 24%
        `the resident floor` MEANS
            `the tax across` (f's `the chargeable income a resident would have in the same circumstances`) `Table 3` `Table 3 rate above the last band`

§§ `s 42A -- the parenthood rebate`

-- s 42A(2A): a resident with "a first child of the family born to him or her on or after 1 January 2008 who is legitimate at
-- the time of the birth" -- "a rebate of $5,000 against the tax payable"; (1)(a): a second child born on or after 1 January
-- 2004 -- $10,000; (2)(a): "a third or fourth child" born on or after 1 January 2004 -- $20,000; (2B)(a): "a fifth or
-- subsequent child" born on or after 1 January 2008 -- $20,000; in each case "allowed for the year of assessment immediately
-- following the year of the birth".
-- (3): where full effect cannot be given "by reason of an insufficiency of the tax payable ..., the balance of the unabsorbed
-- rebate is available for deduction against the tax payable by the individual for the year of assessment immediately
-- following that year of assessment and any subsequent year of assessment."
-- Gloss: a once-off rebate per child against tax, larger for later children, with any unused part carried forward.
-- Only the legitimate-birth limbs (paragraph (a) of each subsection) are encoded; the limbs for a later marriage and for
-- adoption, and the sharing between parents under s 42A(2C) (by agreement, or as the Comptroller thinks reasonable), are not.
GIVEN `I am resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child's place in the family` IS A NUMBER
      `the year the child was born` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What parenthood rebate is allowed to me for this child` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I am resident in Singapore` THEN 0
        IF `the child's place in the family` EQUALS 1 AND `the year the child was born` AT LEAST 2008 THEN 5_000
        IF `the child's place in the family` EQUALS 2 AND `the year the child was born` AT LEAST 2004 THEN 10_000
        IF `the child's place in the family` AT LEAST 3
           AND `the child's place in the family` AT MOST 4 AND `the year the child was born` AT LEAST 2004 THEN 20_000
        IF `the child's place in the family` AT LEAST 5 AND `the year the child was born` AT LEAST 2008 THEN 20_000
        OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the year the child was born` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For which year of assessment is the rebate first allowed` IS `the year the child was born` PLUS 1

GIVEN `my tax payable` IS A NUMBER
      `my unabsorbed rebate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my tax after the parenthood rebate` IS
    `my tax payable` MINUS `the lesser of` `my tax payable` `my unabsorbed rebate`

GIVEN `my tax payable` IS A NUMBER
      `my unabsorbed rebate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much rebate do I carry forward` IS
    `my unabsorbed rebate` MINUS `the lesser of` `my tax payable` `my unabsorbed rebate`
